From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 05:38:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/29] wayland: disconnect clients after the compositor
 prepares to shut down

The Wayland compositor connects to prepare-compositor-shutdown before
the plugin manager exists, so its handler ran first. It stops Xwayland,
which unmanages every X11 window with a destroy effect while the plugin
manager still starts effects. By then the shell has torn itself down, so
the plugin was called into a shell that no longer exists and crashed.

Run the Wayland handler after the others, so the plugin manager stops
starting effects before any client or X11 window goes away.
---
 src/wayland/meta-wayland.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/wayland/meta-wayland.c b/src/wayland/meta-wayland.c
index d78b904127c9d83009c426dfba16c151f50e3637..06ef2b4cd7975828bb55ec6c0a4e14c7245e0b86 100644
--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland.c
@@ -954,8 +954,9 @@ meta_wayland_compositor_new (MetaContext *context)
   compositor = g_object_new (META_TYPE_WAYLAND_COMPOSITOR, NULL);
   compositor->context = context;
 
-  g_signal_connect (context, "prepare-compositor-shutdown",
-                    G_CALLBACK (on_prepare_compositor_shutdown), compositor);
+  g_signal_connect_after (context, "prepare-compositor-shutdown",
+                          G_CALLBACK (on_prepare_compositor_shutdown),
+                          compositor);
 
   wl_display_set_default_max_buffer_size (compositor->wayland_display,
                                           1024 * 1024);
